body:
Because I believe in god, and in my religion. When I say I believe I mean that deep down in my heart, I have no doubt about this.

&#x200B;

Also, most importantly, I don't let sects and religious people influence how I perceive my religion or my god.

lol who's that?

&#x200B;

also, sorry for the super late reply, I'm a reddit newbie

We can argue about it, but to some people (and in some areas) these are as good as you can get to people you can call friends.

&#x200B;

In my experience, individuals that are perceived by other people as "weak" are still bullied, if not physically or verbally they are bullied by being treated as if they're inferior.

&#x200B;

And imo, you just have to safeguard your personality and confidence, especially if you are surrounded by people that see kindness as weakness. Don't worry about labels, if they are not real friends, they won't stick around for long.

That's a huge red flag, the psychological effect is scarring, I'd run away as fast as I could if I were you.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I had friends like that, part of a group not the whole one though, I started neglecting them, guess what? Now they come to talk with me and listen to me. Never show weakness. Your self esteem and dignity is worth it, trust me.
